From 3b530c55e05bda4144e782961b77cea938254c45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:51:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the tab is "DNS Failover", and the ECS note says what
 actually leaves

"Failover" on its own reads as WAN failover, which is a different feature on a
different page. Name it for what it fails over: DNS.

The EDNS Client Subnet switch sends the complete client address, not a
shortened prefix, and add_edns0_config runs once when the query is received -
before an upstream is chosen - so it is attached to every forwarded query,
including any that reach a public fallback server while the owner's own filter
is unavailable. That last part is the half nothing strips, and the help text
now says so: turn it on only when the DNS server receiving it is one you run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
